From: PowOS <powos@powback.com>
Subject: [PATCH] scene: the desktop window never counts as opaque (PowOS phone)

The phone desktop is transparent over Android's wallpaper (org.powos.transparent),
but plasmashell's surface declares an opaque region, so the output under it was
never cleared and translucent pixels accumulated frame after frame (selection
rectangles left trails, like a won game of solitaire).
---
--- a/src/scene/workspacescene.cpp
+++ b/src/scene/workspacescene.cpp
@@ -628,7 +628,12 @@
         effects->prePaintWindow(painted_delegate, windowItem->effectWindow(), data);
 
         Region opaque;
-        if (window->opacity() == 1.0 && !(data.mask & PAINT_WINDOW_TRANSLUCENT)) {
+        // HACK(PowOS phone): the desktop window never counts as opaque. On the phone the desktop is transparent over
+        // Android's wallpaper (org.powos.transparent), but plasmashell's surface still declares itself opaque, so
+        // nothing cleared the output under it and translucent pixels piled up frame after frame (selection
+        // rectangles left trails). Real fix: plasmashell/QtWayland shouldn't set an opaque region on a window
+        // whose color is transparent.
+        if (window->opacity() == 1.0 && !(data.mask & PAINT_WINDOW_TRANSLUCENT) && !window->isDesktop()) {
             addOpaqueRegionRecursive(painted_delegate, windowItem, std::nullopt, opaque);
         }
         m_paintContext.phase2Data.append(Phase2Data{
